From 606a50534c7a3d1a4c050438c216f6d5e496d9ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 19:27:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(agents): canonical role manifest + symmetric
 .claude/.cursor subagent renderers (802aa4d8)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Close the "agents" (subagent role mapping) parity gap that #311 honestly
downgraded to not-delivered/unsupported for every harness.

- Canonical role manifest: agents/<role>.md is the single source of truth for
  Forge's real /dev roles (implementer, spec_reviewer, quality_reviewer — the
  runtime audit roles in lib/commands/dev.js), each with name+description
  frontmatter and a markdown system-prompt body.
- lib/agents-renderer.js emits SYMMETRIC subagent files from that one manifest:
  .claude/agents/<role>.md and .cursor/agents/<role>.md share identical
  name+description frontmatter (the intersection both Claude Code and Cursor
  recognize, per vendor docs), and Codex gets skill-backed
  .codex/skills/<role>/SKILL.md. Built on the `yaml` production dependency
  (never gray-matter). Wired into `forge setup`.
- Matrix: claude+cursor agents rows flipped not-delivered -> native, codex ->
  fallback (skill-backed), hermes stays unsupported; adds sources S11 (Claude
  subagents) + S12 (Cursor subagents). Respects STATUS_VOCABULARY.
- Gitignore .claude/agents + .cursor/agents (generated at setup, like skills);
  ship agents/ in package files. Refresh D20 bd call-site artifact (line shift).

Tests: test/agents-renderer.test.js (manifest load, valid frontmatter, symmetry
across harnesses, codex skill-backing, idempotence) + matrix assertions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
